        "extra_snippets": [
          "Danny Ocean performs during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Group A match between Mexico and South Africa at Mexico City Stadium on June 11, 2026. Luke Hales / Getty Images · Ocean, who was accompanied by colorfully-dressed dancers from the Ballet Folklórico de México, performed his official FIFA World Cup track “Partidazo,\" which is also featured on the tournament's album. ... The Labubu craze has made its way to the World Cup. In between a performance by Belinda and one by J Balvin to kick off the World Cup at Estadio Azteca in Mexico City, the furry sensations that became a must-have accessory in 2025 made an appearance.",
          "Performers dance during the Opening Ceremony ahead of the FIFA World Cup 2026 Group A match between Mexico and South Africa at Mexico City Stadium on June 11, 2026 in Mexico City. Hector Vivas - FIFA / FIFA via Getty Images ... Alejandro Fernández is taking in Estadio Azteca, the Mexico City stadium where the 2026 World Cup kick off is taking place.",
          "The opening ceremonies begins at 1:30 p.m. ET on June 11 inside Estadio Azteca in Mexico City, Mexico. ... The 2026 FIFA World Cup kicks off on June 11 with its first opening ceremony at 10:30 a.m. PT/1:30 p.m.",
          "A recap of the 2026 FIFA World Cup opening ceremony in Mexico City that included Shakira, Burna Boy, Mana, J Balvin and more. All of today’s biggest goals as the first match kicked off."
