        "extra_snippets": [
          "South Africa, ranked 60th and playing their first World Cup match since 2010, is looking forward to a fantastic experience as they expect to make a mark at the",
          "A glittering opening ceremony at the iconic Estadio Azteca in Mexico City marked the start of the FIFA World Cup 2026 on June 11, celebrating football, music and the shared heritage of hosts Mexico, the United States and Canada.",
          "One of the highlights of the FIFA World Cup 2026 opening ceremony at the Azteca Stadium in Mexico was a high energy perfomance by Colombian star Shakira. Shakira and Nigerian singer Burna Boy performed \"Dai Dai,\" the official song of the tournament, bringing roars from the crowd. ... The largest World Cup in tournament history kicks off Thursday with co-host Mexico taking on South Africa in the opening match.",
          "Thousands of football fans attempted to shove their way into Mexico City's official World Cup fan zone on Thursday, creating chaotic scenes shortly before kick-off in the opening game. Access to the fan fest in Zocala plaza was hampered by metal barriers erected in recent days to prevent protesting teachers reaching the area. \"Stop pushing and shoving, there are children here, you're like animals!\" a city official shouted through a megaphone as he tried to control access to the fan venue where the Mexico-South Africa game at the city's Azteca Stadium will be shown on a giant screen."
